    "body": "In the Electrek Podcast , we discuss the most popular news in the world of sustainable transport and energy. In this week’s episode, we’ll discuss Tesla’s earnings, new BYD Seagull, Mustang Mach-E update, and more.\nThe show is live every Friday at 4 p.m. ET on Electrek ’s YouTube channel .\nAs a reminder, we’ll have an accompanying post, like this one, on the site with an embedded link to the live stream. Head to the YouTube channel to get your questions and comments in.\nAfter the show ends at around 5 p.m. ET, the video will be archived on YouTube and the audio on all your favorite podcast apps:\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nApple Podcasts\nSpotify\nOvercast\nPocket Casts\nCastro\nRSS\nWe now have a Patreon if you want to help us avoid more ads and invest more in our content. We have some awesome gifts for our Patreons and more coming.\nHere are a few of the articles that we will discuss during the podcast:\nTesla (TSLA) releases Q3 2026 financial results: margins rebound, profit still falls Tesla blames battery supply for flat sales, but its prices keep falling Tesla FSD ‘subscriptions’ hit 1.74M, counted the way Musk’s pay package wants Tesla energy revenue drops 16% as it refunds customers over tariffs Tesla pushes unsupervised FSD to Q2 2027, and only inside Robotaxi zones Tesla (TSLA) quietly cuts 2026 capex guidance to $20B Tesla pushes Optimus deliveries to late 2027, says hands still a problem Tesla now says it needs its own maps for FSD after years of dismissing maps Tesla skipped the most important shareholder question on its earnings call\nBYD launches new Seagull EV with 5-minute Flash Charging, starting under $10,000\nThe 2027 Ford Mustang Mach-E gains a standard long-range battery and starts at $40,000\nVolvo is launching a ‘lower-priced’ EV in 2027 based on its SPA3 platform\nHuawei’s car unit joins CATL’s 2,520-station battery swap network\nHere’s the live stream for today’s episode starting at 4:00 p.m. ET (or the video after 5 p.m. ET):\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on X , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
